Example of a table of data (dataset)
  Input (A): Size of House (Sq. Ft)
    # of Bedrooms added to A
  Output (B): Price ($1000)

It is up to us to decide what is A and B depending on our use case. 
Ex. Buying a house on a budget
  Input (A): Price ($1000)
  Output (B): Size of House (Sq. Ft) AND # of Bedrooms

Acquiring data
  Manual Labeling 
    Collecting and Labeling data
  Observing Behavious
    Collecting identifiable data (UserID, time)
    Making changes periodically and documenting result (Changing price -> Purchased? (0/1)
    Ex. Machine Number
    Recording Temperature and Pressure to predict if Machine will or will not have a fault (0/1)

Open Internet = Download massive data sets from websites/partnerships that already have collected raw data

Mis-use of data
  Not feeding data to AI software until there "is enough data" or "perfect enough data" to submit
    Start feeding data to AI software quickly
  BUT don't throw data at an AI tema assuming it will be valuable
    Not every data point is valuable

Data is messy 
  If there is bad data then the AI will learn "bad" or incorrect concepts
  Data might include incorrect labels or missing values that need to be cleaned up first before feeding to AI
  There are multiple type of data
    Images, audio, and text are unstructured data
    Structured data are usually data already labeled and in rows and columns or may already have meaning to the data team. 
